# Styling — Tailwind + design tokens

This project uses **Tailwind CSS** with the **Glass Aurora** theme: dark midnight
background, frosted glass panels, soft aurora glows, violet/cyan/pink accents.

## Design tokens

- **Colors are CSS custom properties** defined in `src/styles/global.css`, as
  RGB channels (`--bg-rgb: 11 16 32`) so Tailwind opacity modifiers work
  (`text-ink/60`, `bg-glass/6`).
- **Semantic colors only.** Use `bg`, `ink`, `glass`, and `a1`–`a4` wired
  through `tailwind.config.js`. Never hard-code hex/rgb values in components or
  className strings.
- **Dark-only.** Glass Aurora is a single dark aesthetic; no light/dark toggle.

## Reusable component classes

Defined in `global.css`; prefer these over re-deriving utility soup:
`.card` / `.card--hero`, `.btn` / `.btn--ghost`, `.chip` / `.chip--btn` /
`.chip--active`, `.grad-text`, `.nav-link` / `.nav-link--active`, `.font-display` /
`.kicker`, `.fill-a1`–`.fill-a4`, `.aurora-bg`, `.rise`.

## Layout conventions

- Section wrapper: `max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-20`
- Section kicker/label: `kicker mb-3`
- Section heading: `font-display text-4xl sm:text-5xl`
- Project/listing grids are responsive 1 → 2 → 3 columns.
- Generous dark spacing between glass panels.

## Rules

- **Tokens before new values.** Adding a color or shadow means adding a CSS
  variable + a Tailwind mapping, not inlining a literal.
- **Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`** for entrance animations (`.rise`).
- **Keep `tailwind.config.js` and `global.css` in sync** — every semantic color
  in the config must resolve to a defined CSS variable.
- Global styles are imported once via `gatsby-browser.js`
  (`import "./src/styles/global.css"`); don't import CSS into individual
  components.
- Gradients are glow and text accents only — never flat card backgrounds.
